# Forms: react-hook-form + Zod + Ant Design

## Stack (non-negotiable)
- **react-hook-form** for form state. Never use `useState` to manage form fields manually.
- **Zod v4** (`import { z } from 'zod/v4'`) for validation schemas.
- **`@hookform/resolvers/zod`** to connect them.
- **Ant Design** inputs (`Input`, `Select`, `InputNumber`, `Checkbox`, etc.) as the UI layer.

## Ant Design inputs MUST use Controller

Ant Design components do not forward refs to native inputs. `register()` silently fails — the form sees empty values while the UI shows typed text.

```tsx
// WRONG — register() does not work with Ant Design Input
<Input {...form.register('name')} />

// RIGHT — Controller with explicit value/onChange
<Controller
  control={form.control}
  name="name"
  render={({ field }) => (
    <Input
      value={field.value}
      onChange={(e) => field.onChange(e.target.value)}
      onBlur={field.onBlur}
    />
  )}
/>
```

For non-event controls (Select, InputNumber, Checkbox):
```tsx
<Controller
  control={form.control}
  name="status"
  render={({ field }) => (
    <Select value={field.value} onChange={field.onChange} options={[...]} />
  )}
/>
```

## Schema location and naming
- One file per entity: `src/schemas/<entity>.ts`
- Export the schema and the inferred type:

```ts
export const campaignSchema = z.object({ ... })
export type CampaignFormData = z.infer<typeof campaignSchema>
```

- Schema fields MUST match the OpenAPI `definition.yaml` contract. Check `../admin/api/v2/data/definition.yaml` (from this package in the self-hosted repo) before defining fields.

## Form layout
- Wrap every labeled field in `<FormField>` from `@/components/ui-kit` — it handles label, error display, and help text.
- Error message: `form.formState.errors.<field>?.message`

## Modal forms pattern
```tsx
<Modal open={open} onCancel={onClose} title="..." footer={null} width={640} destroyOnHidden>
  <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="space-y-6 pt-4">
    {/* fields */}
    <div className="flex gap-2 pt-4">
      <Button type="primary" htmlType="submit" disabled={isSubmitting} className="flex-1">
        {isSubmitting && <Loader2 className="mr-2 h-4 w-4 animate-spin" />}
        {initialData ? 'Save' : 'Create'}
      </Button>
      <Button htmlType="button" onClick={onClose} className="flex-1">Cancel</Button>
    </div>
  </form>
</Modal>
```

## Reset on open/edit
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (open) {
    form.reset(initialData ? mapToFormData(initialData) : defaultValues)
  }
}, [open, initialData, form])
```

## Array fields
- For key-value lists: use `KeyValueListField` with `form.watch()` + `form.setValue(..., { shouldDirty: true })`.
- For complex arrays: use `useFieldArray` from react-hook-form.

## Never
- Never build form state with `useState` per field.
- Never validate manually with if-chains — use Zod schema.
- Never use `register()` with Ant Design components — always `Controller`.
- Never skip `FormField` wrapper — it provides consistent error display.
